# Production Hardening Implementation Plan

## Goal
Harden the `Nucleus` (GentleQuest Backend) application for production by verifying Rate Limiting and implementing strict Security Headers.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> **HSTS Enabled**: logic will likely force HTTPS. Ensure your local dev environment can handle this or that the logic excludes `localhost`.

## Proposed Changes

### [Backend]
#### [MODIFY] [app.py](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/app.py)
- **Add Security Headers Middleware**: Implement an `@app.after_request` hook to inject standard security headers.
  - `Strict-Transport-Security`: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains (Production only)
  - `X-Content-Type-Options`: nosniff
  - `X-Frame-Options`: SAMEORIGIN
  - `X-XSS-Protection`: 1; mode=block
  - `Referrer-Policy`: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  - `Content-Security-Policy`: upgrade-insecure-requests (Optional/Basic)

- **Verify Rate Limiting**: Ensure `RATELIMIT_ENABLED` is respected and limits are appropriate ([Config](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/app.py#295-385) class).

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- **Curl Headers Check**:
  ```bash
  curl -I http://localhost:5055/api/health
  ```
  *Expect*: All security headers present. HSTS only if HTTPS or forced.

### Manual Verification
- **Browser Check**: Open Chrome DevTools -> Network -> Headers on the live app (once deployed) or local.
